A||||1||Ken Wittlief||Running rich? Not anymore! Yeah Baby Yeah!||||1||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||05-21-2001||11:55 PM||||My car is fixed and it is running sooooo sweet!<P>I was geting code 45 - O2 rich - at idle, and code 33 - MAP sensor - at startup.<P>  I found the vacuum hose under the plenium that had creature damage - and a crack in the egr tube.<P>  So I replaced the vacuum tube (c: and I brazed the egr tube with MAP gas and my swirl port torch - put new gaskets on, and repainted the plenium in the process.<P>  So THIS is how a V6 fiero is suppose to run! Awesome! I had my first spinout tonight. Its been raining on and off, and I was driving to get the ECM to recalibrate, made a left at an intersection and punched it halfway through the turn.<P>  You cant do that in a fiero! Both back wheels broke loose and it started to spin out. It was totally unexpected, but from years of driving in the snow up here i instinctively steered into the slide, over corrected once and managed to recover while mostly staying in my lane.<P>  Fortunately government protection of our fine citizens was a little lacking in the area.<P>  I cant get over how great the car runs now. Since I already started by painting the plenium, will have to get busy on the rest of the car now (paint) - looks like my drivetrain is in good shape.<P>  One thing I noticed that is odd, though. When speeding up to around 40mph or so, and letting off to hold speed, I hear something running, kinda of RRRRrrrrrrrrrr sound, almost like the heater is switching from vents to floor or like a power window is going up, that kind of sound. I have no idea what it could be?! the fuel pump doesnt cycle on and off, does it? I dont think its the radiator fan.<P>  Could it be a valve in the auto tranny. Maybe the tranny needs an oil and filter change, and maintaince adjustment. I cant figure out what the sound is.<P>  Other than that, my car is like a whole new beast now! cant wait to see what my mpg's go up to. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||gixxer||05-22-2001||12:17 AM||||Glad you got it sorted out. <BR>Just went thru that exercise yesterday. <BR>Ended up putting little spring hose clamps on all the connections. <BR>Makes a BIG difference. <BR>||||reg||14
